1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
drifting over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,860
I kicked a pebble and it
flew up through the clouds,

3
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:29,360
to the Kashiwa gym where I was out jogging,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,740
they laughed at me for
staying so full of energy.

5
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
it's only serious,
and there's a stockpile of it.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, and the unchanging streetscape,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
are gentler than before.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are crying,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,940
the ponzu will give us some, won't it.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,940
Stuffing our cheeks with yakitori,

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:54,620
is it also something to look at?

13
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointy hat...

14
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,560
Enjoy the comedy

15
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,500
Approaching Minami-Senju.

16
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:41,360
Doors on the left toward Ueno.

17
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:43,420
Looks like a real showdown at 3:03:27.

18
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:46,040
I'm curious about the No.
12 Ikkakusen Chika.

19
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:53,800
Right, right.

20
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,180
That's right.

21
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:58,140
Hey, young man! This is the priority seat!

22
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:00,060
I'm going to take those two seats this year!

23
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:01,220
Wait a moment.

24
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:02,480
Shut up!

25
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:03,620
What did you say?

26
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:08,080
Alright, let's go!

27
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,360
Here you go.

28
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,180
Thank you very much.

29
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:13,200
You're welcome.

30
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:19,820
It feels good after doing a good deed.

31
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:23,860
Feeling great here, striking it rich...
striking it rich, just kidding.

32
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,320
You old geezer!

33
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:33,960
Hey.

34
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:46,920
It's me, it's me.

35
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,260
I was planning to beat
up some annoying old man.

36
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,540
Hey, old man, wait up.

37
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,360
You guys, from earlier -

38
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:04,380
Mind if we have a little word with you?

39
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:07,440
Unfortunately,
my face isn't removable, you know.

40
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:09,820
Don't mess with me, get over here!

41
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:20,720
Ryo-san!

42
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:25,740
Are you going to the races?

43
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:27,300
I'm off duty, you know.

44
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,880
Patrol must be tough

45
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:30,320
Good luck out there.

46
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,120
Ryo-san, if you win, you've got to treat us.

47
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,200
So you're a police officer?

48
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:37,940
Just you watch.

49
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:40,100
You idiot!

50
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:43,880
What's the meaning of picking a
fight with five high school students?

51
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:45,440
Please, wait.

52
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:47,420
Chief, it's not my fault.

53
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,140
That was self-defense.

54
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,420
They even filed a complaint
claiming it wasn't self-defense.

55
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:54,600
Honestly, you're something else.

56
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,900
But...

57
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:59,680
Either way,
I'm ordering you to stay home for a week.

58
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,760
That's all.

59
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:02,600
Chief...

60
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:06,560
Senpai,
there's no point arguing any further.

61
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,540
We're lucky it was only
a week of house confinement

62
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:12,340
because the Chief bowed his head to so
many people behind the scenes for us.

63
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,860
Damn those brats!

64
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:18,200
Alright, if that's how it is,

65
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:20,980
So, senpai,
you're not seriously going to take revenge?!

66
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,640
Let's go all out and build plastic models!

67
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:24,880
Ugh...

68
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:31,200
That old man got a week of house arrest!

69
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:35,280
Hahaha! Serves him right! Good for him!

70
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:40,240
Wait!

71
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,760
W-who are you guys!

72
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:48,792
I'm glad you asked.

73
00:04:48,842 --> 00:04:52,398
We are Jijurenger Blue,

74
00:04:52,448 --> 00:04:55,504
Jijurenger Yellow,

75
00:04:55,554 --> 00:04:58,659
Jijurenger White,

76
00:04:58,709 --> 00:05:01,512
Jijurenger Blue,

77
00:05:01,562 --> 00:05:04,414
Jijurenger Red,

78
00:05:04,464 --> 00:05:06,093
all five of us together,

79
00:05:06,143 --> 00:05:10,460
the rowdy world's Jijurengers!

80
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,520
Hey, wait a minute!

81
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,280
What is it? Shut up already.

82
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:20,746
Above all, when you rode the subway,

83
00:05:20,796 --> 00:05:23,480
you were sprawled out in the priority seat,
weren't you?

84
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:25,360
So what if I was?

85
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:30,000
And on top of that, you were making
a phone call even though it's banned!

86
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,636
Even if the conductor lets it slide,

87
00:05:32,686 --> 00:05:34,960
the Downtown Anger
Brigade won't stand for it!

88
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:38,560
On behalf of the Kameari Kōen-mae
Police Box in Katsushika Ward,

89
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:41,640
Shut up already!

90
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:44,500
Are you alright?

91
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:45,960
I'm fine.

92
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,560
Hey, young man!

93
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:50,160
Looks like you've really made us angry.

94
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:52,020
Green-san, go ahead and get him!

95
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:53,860
Yes, Lord Elder!

96
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,720
What, you want a fight?

97
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:04,440
If you're finished with
your little tantrum...

98
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,540
Finally got it, I tell you!

99
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,540
So you're not going to fight, then?

100
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:12,720
Come on, everyone, get him!

101
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:17,140
What do you think you're doing?

102
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:18,820
This is the final touch!

103
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:40,260
Justice always prevails!

104
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:41,216
We are,

105
00:06:41,266 --> 00:06:44,760
the Downtown Angry Force, Jijurengers!

106
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:46,680
W-what is it?

107
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:50,314
Sprawling around in a slovenly manner
even though you're a middle schooler,

108
00:06:50,364 --> 00:06:52,065
smoking cigarettes and such,

109
00:06:52,115 --> 00:06:55,140
people like that need punishment!
Rubber set!

110
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:03,105
Even if the convenience
store clerk forgives you,

111
00:07:03,155 --> 00:07:06,040
we Downtown Angry Force won't forgive you!
Let's go!

112
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,800
What if little kids copy this guy?

113
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,240
Cool your head and reflect on yourself!

114
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,820
Now, everyone!

115
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,320
Justice always prevails!

116
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:31,820
We are,

117
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:34,700
the Search Tournament Jigureijaa!

118
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:35,860
Hey, wait!

119
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,060
Let's finish this together!

120
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:38,300
Nooo!

121
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:41,900
You bastard!

122
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:43,900
Ready... set!

123
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:50,395
Learn your lesson,

124
00:07:50,445 --> 00:07:53,520
and don't go browsing dirty
magazines at bookstores!

125
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:55,640
W-what's the big deal? It's just that much!

126
00:07:56,060 --> 00:08:00,100
You've got to pretend you just
bought these with regular books,

127
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:03,800
then lock your door at
home and sneak a peek.

128
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,900
Stop your yapping and hand it over!

129
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,620
Bleh!

130
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:10,340
Bleh bleh, bottoms up!

131
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,900
Well then, shall we be off?

132
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:14,620
Phew, that really wore me out.

133
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:16,020
Wow, seriously...

134
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:17,760
Oh my.

135
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:20,280
It's the Shitamachi Angry Brigade!

136
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,180
How about it?

137
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:24,100
Oh no, oh no, oh no!

138
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:24,500
Uh-oh, uh-oh!

139
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:28,000
Justice always wins!

140
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:31,600
We are the Shitamachi Angry Brigade,
Shijuenger!

141
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:33,660
Oh no, oh no!

142
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:36,320
Excuse me,
would you mind joining us in a photo?

143
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,680
Yay!

144
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:38,380
Yeah!

145
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:40,620
Okay!

146
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:43,760
Say cheese!

147
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:44,780
Yeah!

148
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:46,790
This is what's currently

149
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:51,100
causing a stir in society: the members of the Shitamachi Angry Brigade,
the Jijurengers.

150
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:56,720
Some praise them for punishing young
people who don't follow morals and rules,

151
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:59,560
but victims have complained
that they go too far.

152
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:04,760
Also, they reportedly say they're taking the place of
the Kameari Kōen-mae police box and delivering punishment.

153
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:08,020
We can't just overlook this either.

154
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:10,580
Detain them as soon as you find them.

155
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:15,900
What's wrong, Reiko-san?

156
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:18,860
That Jijuren Green...
doesn't he look like someone?

157
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:25,620
R-Ryotsu?! Isn't that Ryotsu!

158
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,060
Ugh...

159
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,400
Ugh... there, that's better.

160
00:09:34,020 --> 00:09:35,880
Who's there? Shut up already!

161
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,020
It's me!

162
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,180
Y-you should!

163
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:40,080
What on earth happened...?

164
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:44,080
What, what, what?
Hey, what do you think you're doing!

165
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,840
Ryotsu! I misjudged you!

166
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:49,800
Out of spite for your house arrest, you
dragged your comrades into this nonsense!

167
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,880
We're the Shitamachi Angry Brigade,
the Jijurengers!

168
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:57,780
Shitamachi Angry Brigade? Jijurengers?
What's that supposed to be?

169
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:01,120
Even now, you still intend to play dumb?

170
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:05,280
Wait, wait, wait!
I really don't know anything!

171
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:06,980
Even after seeing this,
you still claim you know nothing?

172
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:12,040
I would never wear such
an embarrassing outfit!

173
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:16,540
Are you sure this isn't
revenge for your suspension?

174
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:22,580
Don't be ridiculous! I was suspended, and
I made this without leaving the dorm once!

175
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,080
You made all of this?

176
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:29,500
That's right. Do you think I had time
to go out and waste it on such nonsense?

177
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:30,840
Chief.

178
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:36,120
If it comes to this,
I'll prove my innocence myself.

179
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:39,620
I'll catch those Shitamachi Angry
Brigade bastards with my own hands!

180
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,780
Fine, if you're so sure of yourself,
go ahead and catch them!

181
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:43,420
Yes, sir!

182
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:49,602
The Jijurengers appeared

183
00:10:49,652 --> 00:10:52,400
within a 3-kilometer
radius centered on Asakusa.

184
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:53,228
Ryo-sama,

185
00:10:53,278 --> 00:10:57,560
so we just need to patrol
that area thoroughly, right?

186
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:01,224
That's right! Listen up! Those punks
who don't follow the rules of society,

187
00:11:01,274 --> 00:11:03,080
keep a close eye on them!

188
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:04,100
Yes!

189
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:30,100
Honestly, what a nuisance.

190
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,700
Should we call everyone together?

191
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:36,340
Listen!
Smoking by minors is prohibited by law!

192
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:39,160
Don't you dare smoke again! Now get going!

193
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:40,080
Yes.

194
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,100
Honestly.

195
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:45,440
It's me!

196
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,180
Ryo-sama, he's finally shown up!

197
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,280
Where am I?

198
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:49,840
We're in the precincts of a shrine.

199
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,500
Got it! On my way!

200
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:54,980
Nakagawa, can you hear me?

201
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,780
The Shitamachi Angry Brigade
is on the shrine grounds.

202
00:11:58,760 --> 00:11:59,620
Hahahaha!

203
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:02,900
Stop it!

204
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:04,780
Had enough?

205
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:05,920
Youngster!

206
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:08,360
On behalf of Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box,

207
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,020
Punishment!

208
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:09,660
That's enough!

209
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:12,200
Don't move!

210
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:24,920
There's no escape now.

211
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:25,740
Give up.

212
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,520
It's Natchi of Momus!

213
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,580
Damn it!

214
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:47,160
Chase Maria White, I'll chase Asia Green.

215
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:47,640
Understood.

216
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:51,980
Shit.

217
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:56,940
Hey, wait!

218
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,800
The bastard's hiding somewhere.

219
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:11,120
Yo, Kankichi, what the hell are you doing?

220
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:14,080
A cop peeping into other people's houses?

221
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:15,640
Hey, Gen-san the tatami maker.

222
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:17,560
What, you're still alive?

223
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:21,500
As you can see, I'm fit as a fiddle,
and I'm working like crazy too.

224
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:23,240
That's good to hear.

225
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:24,480
By the way, Gen-san.

226
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:27,800
Did you see some weird
guy wearing green tights?

227
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:31,600
I just finished work and came out.

228
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,220
I see.

229
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:33,700
Did something happen?

230
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:38,840
Well, a group has appeared that scolds
young people who don't follow society's rules.

231
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:42,180
That would've been a common story back in the old days,
wouldn't it?

232
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:46,140
Speaking of which, Gen-san used to
hit me all the time when I was young.

233
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:48,740
Well, that's because you
lot were up to no good.

234
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:52,560
No, I did misbehave sometimes, but he hit
me even when I hadn't done anything wrong.

235
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:55,280
Like the time I got yelled at for
taking persimmons from Gen-san's house.

236
00:13:55,280 --> 00:14:01,400
He said if you want persimmons, come and ask openly,
so I did just that, and he went and hit me anyway, didn't he!

237
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:02,540
Was that so?

238
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,700
I don't have time for this idle chatter.

239
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:07,880
Well then, see you.

240
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:13,380
How did it go?

241
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:16,540
I had them cornered in a vacant lot, but

242
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:18,540
I fell into a pitfall trap.

243
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:22,680
I thought I had them cornered
in a dead-end alley too.

244
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:26,540
But it was just an old gardener,
and I let them get away.

245
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:27,800
An old man?

246
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:31,020
When I lost sight of them,
I ran into an old man too.

247
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:34,500
Now that you mention it, me too.
I ran into an old man, Senpai.

248
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,240
Ryo-chan, what's wrong?

249
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:44,460
No, it's nothing.
Sorry for making you help me today.

250
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:47,080
I'll handle it alone from tomorrow. See you.

251
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,620
No, wait a second, Senpai.

252
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:57,100
Something about that old
geezer Kanbei is bugging me.

253
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:04,960
Goddamn old geezer,
still living it up as flashy as ever!

254
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:31,720
Mm.

255
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:33,240
Mm.

256
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,760
Mm.

257
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,220
Mm.

258
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,360
Mm.

259
00:15:49,060 --> 00:15:50,460
Mm.

260
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:51,640
Mm.

261
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:51,680
Mm.

262
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:51,780
Mm.

263
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:51,820
Mm.

264
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:01,080
What are those guys doing?

265
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:09,000
Phone calls disturb the other guests.

266
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:12,300
Please set your phone to silent
mode and refrain from calls.

267
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:14,540
Looks like nobody can hear it.

268
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:15,800
Shall we do one more?

269
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,500
Gen-san, pull yourself together!

270
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:23,880
Ginza's heart is bad,
so he's wearing a pacemaker.

271
00:16:24,260 --> 00:16:25,660
Hang up your phone quickly!

272
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,680
Are you all right, Ginza?

273
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:31,420
Somehow.

274
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:35,020
Those old geezers really go all out.

275
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:43,880
Even after all that,
there's still someone who never learns

276
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:45,660
What should we do, Kanbei?

277
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:48,800
No choice, shall we use that thing?

278
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,800
Hello? Hello? Hello? Hello?

279
00:16:58,580 --> 00:16:59,980
Damn, it cut off.

280
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:04,340
We're aboveground,
so why is it showing out of area?

281
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:09,460
They used a machine to knock out phone signals.
Those old geezers are terrifying.

282
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:23,980
No mistake about it, right?

283
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,400
Going by the numbers,
it has to be those guys.

284
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,960
But we need solid, undeniable evidence.

285
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,540
It's him.

286
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,580
What, really?

287
00:17:32,580 --> 00:17:33,200
Good.

288
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:37,920
Are you sure there's no mistake?

289
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,800
I'm sure the corpse had a mole.

290
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:49,600
Just as I thought, it's him.

291
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:52,220
I got a good look at the mole on the corpse.

292
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:55,820
The old men's expressions
suddenly turned grim.

293
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,160
Just as I thought,

294
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,440
wait!

295
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:29,940
Who are you lot?

296
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:32,500
Glad you asked!

297
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,560
We are

298
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:38,320
Jijirengers Euro!

299
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:41,940
Jijirengers White!

300
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:45,040
Jijirengers Blue!

301
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,840
Jijirengers Red!

302
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:50,060
Five strong, together,

303
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:53,480
Trickster Fleet, Jijurengers!

304
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:55,620
Get out of the way.

305
00:18:55,620 --> 00:18:57,180
Not so fast.

306
00:18:57,180 --> 00:19:00,080
A week ago, on the Hibiya Line subway,

307
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:02,940
you told off an old man for
talking on his cell phone,

308
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:06,240
then chased him down and pushed him down the stairs,
didn't you?

309
00:19:06,860 --> 00:19:08,340
I don't know anything about that.

310
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:12,140
Don't lie. Do you recognize this face?

311
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:15,380
You're the one who -

312
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:20,040
You were with Ume-san, the one who
was pushed down the stairs that time.

313
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:23,440
Hold it, old man!

314
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:29,020
Hey, old man,
you made a fool of me on the train earlier!

315
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:31,680
Stop it! You're the one who's in the wrong!

316
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:38,220
Are you all right? Pull yourself together!

317
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:42,100
Sis hasn't been able to play

318
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:44,800
her beloved gateball since that injury.

319
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:47,800
I see. So that's how it was.

320
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:51,800
That old man just tripped and fell on his own,
didn't he?

321
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:53,940
Are you planning to brazen it out?

322
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:55,760
So what if we are?

323
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:59,340
On behalf of the Kameari Park Police Box,
Katsushika Ward,

324
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,720
it's time for punishment!

325
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:03,180
Eeeehhhh!

326
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:03,500
Mm.

327
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:10,460
Hey, hey, hey, what's the matter with you?
Can't be helped.

328
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:14,680
Ugh! Ugh!

329
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:16,620
Get out of the way! If you don't move,
you'll get seriously hurt.

330
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:17,440
Wait!

331
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:20,080
Come on, Heart!

332
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:23,140
Jijurenger Black, reporting for duty!

333
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:25,320
Ugh!

334
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:26,080
Yaaah!

335
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:27,820
Come on!

336
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:29,640
Ugh!

337
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:35,840
See? Surrender! This is what happens
when you mess with Jijurenger Black!

338
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:38,400
Looks like Jijurenger Black has shown up

339
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,780
I don't know anything about it!

340
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:42,840
Don't mind that, just go for it!

341
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:56,980
Right then, here we go!

342
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:16,420
On behalf of the Kameari Park police box,
this is your punishment!

343
00:21:23,940 --> 00:21:24,980
Learned your lesson?

344
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:27,500
This is nothing compared to Ume-san's pain!

345
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:29,600
Everyone, tickle attack!

346
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:38,760
Oh crap!

347
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:40,820
Stop, stop!

348
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:41,240
Hey!

349
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:42,280
Stop!

350
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:42,940
Stop it, stop it!

351
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:45,060
Stop it, stop it!

352
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:45,320
My butt!

353
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:47,940
Stop!

354
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:59,480
Justice always prevails!

355
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,200
We are...

356
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:03,000
the Northern Personality
Challenge Jijurenger!

357
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:06,000
Thanks, Jijurenger Black.

358
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,480
We were saved thanks to you.

359
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:09,260
But by the way, Black...

360
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:10,800
Who the heck are you?

361
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:15,380
Are you satisfied now?

362
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:16,580
Kankichi.

363
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:18,100
Honestly...

364
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,200
At your age, acting like this...

365
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:21,060
Don't go overboard, Kanbe.

366
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:22,260
What?

367
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:24,840
So that's how it is.

368
00:22:29,340 --> 00:22:34,520
What's the big idea? If Kankichi's the one arresting me,
I'm honored, come on.

369
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:40,020
Go ahead, cuff me. I don't know anything.
I just taught that stupid young man a lesson.

370
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:45,720
The Jijurengers are
disbanded as of today. See ya.

371
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:46,500
Mm.

372
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:48,520
Mm.

373
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:55,320
So that's how it was.

374
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:58,220
But resorting to force was wrong.

375
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:00,720
Chief, I'm truly sorry.

376
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:02,140
About those old men...

377
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:05,700
I'll act like I never heard anything.

378
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:06,720
Chief.

379
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:10,060
Forget it. Drink up.

380
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:15,160
Well, then.

381
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:25,240
Back in the day, there were adults who
scolded young people when they misbehaved.

382
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:30,400
When did Japanese adults
forget how to scold the young?

383
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,620
Then I'm a lucky man, aren't I?

384
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:35,640
Because I have a chief who always scolds me.

385
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,100
You idiot!

386
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:37,620
Hey, Chief.

387
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,980
Listen, Ryotsu, don't get the wrong idea.

388
00:23:39,980 --> 00:23:42,880
Your suspension hasn't been lifted yet.

389
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:44,840
Please forgive me, Chief.

390
00:23:46,080 --> 00:23:47,620
Come on, have a drink with me.

391
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:57,860
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out

392
00:23:59,100 --> 00:24:01,860
I walked on, looking back

393
00:24:01,860 --> 00:24:04,480
pulled along by the
clink of gachapon machines

394
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:11,640
that strange feeling I had back then

395
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:16,900
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

396
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:22,660
I tried walking only on the black ones.

397
00:24:25,180 --> 00:24:28,840
Everyone was a child once,

398
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:30,920
but everyone has forgotten.

399
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:34,980
Politicians with their self-important faces,

400
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:38,260
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

401
00:24:38,780 --> 00:24:41,300
Go on, take a turn.

402
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:15,360
Come on over to our town!

403
00:25:16,580 --> 00:25:16,940
Thank you.

404
00:25:19,980 --> 00:25:22,980
Is there really a barbershop that cuts
your hair without taking your money?

405
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:24,200
Let's go, let's go, where is it?

406
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:27,100
It's run by a stubborn old downtown dad.

407
00:25:27,100 --> 00:25:28,360
He's a bit of a nag.

408
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,980
Isn't that just the
kind of place you'd love?

409
00:25:29,980 --> 00:25:32,140
What hairstyle? Only the crew cut!

410
00:25:32,540 --> 00:25:33,180
What's that supposed to mean?

411
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:36,480
Next time, let's spread the circle
of crew cuts across the world!

412
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:37,400
Nice to meet you.

413
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:49,140
Everyone, come on over to our town!

414
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:50,800
Thank you.

